From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clauger 3E <dev@clauger.fr>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ti: icssg-prueth-sr1: open the classifier only once RX
 is ready

emac_ndo_open() programs the default classifier first and boots the
PRU/RTU firmware before the RX channels are enabled and before
napi_enable(). Unlike the SR2 firmware, which forwards nothing until
ICSSG_EMAC_PORT_FORWARD is set on link up, the SR1 firmware pushes
received frames to the host as soon as it runs. With traffic on the wire,
the first RX interrupt can therefore fire while NAPI_STATE_SCHED is still
set by netif_napi_add(): prueth_rx_irq() disables the IRQ, napi_schedule()
does nothing, and the poll that would re-enable the IRQ never runs. RX is
dead until the next open.

Observed on an IOT2050 Advanced (AM65x SR1.0): MAC statistics keep
counting received frames, the RX data IRQ count stays at exactly 1, and
nothing reaches the stack for the whole boot. Reproduced on 4 consecutive
boots with traffic on the port at open time; opening the same port
without link, then plugging the cable, works. With this patch: 14 out of
14 boots with traffic at open time, both ports receiving.

Keep the classifier disabled while the firmware starts and RX is set up,
and program the default classifier only once the RX channels and NAPI
are enabled, mirroring emac_ndo_stop() which disables it first to block
packets from the wire.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/ti/icssg/icssg_prueth_sr1.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/icssg/icssg_prueth_sr1.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/icssg/icssg_prueth_sr1.c
index f88cdc8f012f..cabc49bce869 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/icssg/icssg_prueth_sr1.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/ti/icssg/icssg_prueth_sr1.c
@@ -500,7 +500,13 @@ static int emac_ndo_open(struct net_device *ndev)
 
 	icssg_class_set_mac_addr(prueth->miig_rt, slice, emac->mac_addr);
 
-	icssg_class_default(prueth->miig_rt, slice, 0, true);
+	/* The SR1 firmware pushes frames to the host as soon as it runs: an
+	 * RX interrupt raised before napi_enable() masks the IRQ for good
+	 * (NAPI_STATE_SCHED still set, the poll never runs). Keep frames from
+	 * the wire away until RX channels and NAPI are enabled; the classifier
+	 * is opened then, mirroring emac_ndo_stop().
+	 */
+	icssg_class_disable(prueth->miig_rt, slice);
 
 	/* Notify the stack of the actual queue counts. */
 	ret = netif_set_real_num_tx_queues(ndev, num_data_chn);
@@ -599,6 +605,8 @@ static int emac_ndo_open(struct net_device *ndev)
 		napi_enable(&emac->tx_chns[i].napi_tx);
 	napi_enable(&emac->napi_rx);
 
+	icssg_class_default(prueth->miig_rt, slice, 0, true);
+
 	/* start PHY */
 	phy_start(ndev->phydev);
 
